---
// Part 2 backpropagation: blame flows from the output back to every weight.
---

<svg viewBox="0 0 400 330" width="100%" role="img" aria-labelledby="nnb-bp-t nnb-bp-d">
  <title id="nnb-bp-t">Backpropagation: handing the blame back</title>
  <desc id="nnb-bp-d">
    The same network, with arrows pointing backwards from right to left. At the output, the blame is the guess minus
    the truth: 0.786 minus 1 is minus 0.214. It flows back along the weight of 1.5 to neuron A: minus 0.214 times 1.5 is
    minus 0.321. Neuron B was off, so no blame reaches it. A's blame is multiplied by each of its inputs to give the
    gradients of A's three weights: minus 1.93 for links, minus 1.28 for money words, and 0 for known sender.
  </desc>
  <defs>
    <marker id="nnb-bp-a" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
      <path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10 z" style="fill: var(--viz-warn)" />
    </marker>
  </defs>
  <rect x="300" y="116" width="96" height="68" rx="10" stroke-width="2" style="fill: var(--viz-bad-soft); stroke: var(--viz-bad)" />
  <text x="348" y="138" font-size="15" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" style="fill: var(--viz-ink)">output</text>
  <text x="348" y="158" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" style="fill: var(--viz-muted); font-family: var(--sl-font-mono)">0.786 − 1</text>
  <text x="348" y="177" font-size="16" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" style="fill: var(--viz-warn); font-family: var(--sl-font-mono)">−0.214</text>

  <rect x="160" y="56" width="76" height="68" rx="10" stroke-width="2" style="fill: var(--viz-ok-soft); stroke: var(--viz-ok)" />
  <text x="198" y="80" font-size="15" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" style="fill: var(--viz-ink)">A</text>
  <text x="198" y="108" font-size="16" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" style="fill: var(--viz-warn); font-family: var(--sl-font-mono)">−0.321</text>
  <rect x="160" y="176" width="76" height="68" rx="10" stroke-width="2" style="fill: var(--viz-surface); stroke: var(--viz-stroke)" />
  <text x="198" y="200" font-size="15" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" style="fill: var(--viz-ink)">B</text>
  <text x="198" y="228" font-size="16" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" style="fill: var(--viz-muted); font-family: var(--sl-font-mono)">0</text>

  <line x1="298" y1="140" x2="240" y2="96" stroke-width="2.5" style="stroke: var(--viz-warn)" marker-end="url(#nnb-bp-a)" />
  <text x="276" y="100" font-size="14" style="fill: var(--viz-muted); font-family: var(--sl-font-mono)">×1.5</text>
  <line x1="298" y1="162" x2="240" y2="206" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="4 4" style="stroke: var(--viz-stroke)" />
  <text x="250" y="232" font-size="14" style="fill: var(--viz-muted)">was off:</text>
  <text x="250" y="250" font-size="14" style="fill: var(--viz-muted)">no blame</text>

  <line x1="158" y1="76" x2="112" y2="40" stroke-width="2" style="stroke: var(--viz-warn)" marker-end="url(#nnb-bp-a)" />
  <line x1="158" y1="90" x2="112" y2="118" stroke-width="2" style="stroke: var(--viz-warn)" marker-end="url(#nnb-bp-a)" />
  <line x1="158" y1="104" x2="112" y2="196" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="4 4" style="stroke: var(--viz-stroke)" />
  <text x="4" y="30" font-size="14" style="fill: var(--viz-muted)">links weight</text>
  <text x="4" y="50" font-size="15" font-weight="700" style="fill: var(--viz-warn); font-family: var(--sl-font-mono)">×6 = −1.93</text>
  <text x="4" y="112" font-size="14" style="fill: var(--viz-muted)">money weight</text>
  <text x="4" y="132" font-size="15" font-weight="700" style="fill: var(--viz-warn); font-family: var(--sl-font-mono)">×4 = −1.28</text>
  <text x="4" y="196" font-size="14" style="fill: var(--viz-muted)">known weight</text>
  <text x="4" y="216" font-size="15" font-weight="700" style="fill: var(--viz-muted); font-family: var(--sl-font-mono)">×0 = 0</text>

  <text x="4" y="290" font-size="15" style="fill: var(--viz-ink)">← blame flows backwards; A's −0.321 × each input</text>
  <text x="4" y="314" font-size="15" style="fill: var(--viz-muted)">negative: raise this weight to lower the loss</text>
</svg>
